Here’s a self-contained, responsive login page. It validates that the fields are filled in, but **doesn’t authenticate users**—connect the form to a secure backend to handle real logins.

```html name=login.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Login</title>
  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      padding: 1rem;
      font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
      background: #f3f4f6;
      color: #1f2937;
    }

    .login-card {
      width: min(100%, 400px);
      padding: 2rem;
      background: #fff;
      border-radius: 12px;
      box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgb(0 0 0 / 8%);
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .subtitle {
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
      text-align: center;
      color: #6b7280;
    }

    .field {
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    label {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    input {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
      border-radius: 6px;
      font: inherit;
    }

    input:focus {
      outline: 3px solid #bfdbfe;
      border-color: #2563eb;
    }

    button {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0.8rem;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 6px;
      background: #2563eb;
      color: white;
      font: inherit;
      font-weight: 700;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    button:hover {
      background: #1d4ed8;
    }

    #message {
      min-height: 1.5rem;
      margin: 1rem 0 0;
      text-align: center;
      color: #b91c1c;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="login-card">
    <h1>Welcome back</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Sign in to your account</p>

    <form id="login-form">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="email">Email</label>
        <input
          id="email"
          name="email"
          type="email"
          autocomplete="username"
          required
        />
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label for="password">Password</label>
        <input
          id="password"
          name="password"
          type="password"
          autocomplete="current-password"
          required
        />
      </div>

      <button type="submit">Log in</button>
      <p id="message" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
  </main>

  <script>
    document.querySelector("#login-form").addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      document.querySelector("#message").textContent =
        "Demo only — connect this form to your authentication backend.";
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```
